    "title": "Diabetic Lower Extremity Wounds - HBOTQ",
    "meta_description": "Diabetes is a metabolic disorder that impairs the body\u2019s ability to produce enough insulin, leading to elevated blood glucose levels, which hinder wound healing and increase the risk of infection. Diabetic ulcers, particularly on the legs and feet, can become chronic if not healed within three months. Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy (HBOT) accelerates the healing of these lower extremity wounds, lowers amputation rates, and significantly improves the quality of life for diabetic patients.",
