    "content_type": "text/html",
    "bytes": 458702,
    "title": "Radiation Tissue Damage - HBOTQ",
    "meta_description": "Radiation treatment, commonly used for cancer, can cause necrosis, damaging both healthy and cancerous cells. This damage may lead to non-healing wounds due to impaired blood supply, particularly in delayed radiation injuries that appear six months or more after treatment. Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy (HBOT) helps repair radiation-damaged tissue by promoting blood vessel regeneration, stimulating stem cell growth, and accelerating wound healing. The benefits of HBOT in treating radiation-induced tissue damage have been demonstrated in several controlled studies.",
    "canonical": "https://hbotq.com/condition/radiation-tissue-damage/",
    "robots": "index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1, max-image-preview:large",
